{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "bed_deformation",
    "description": "PISM bed-deformation boundary (stage 2 of the eqice project), model bed_deformation.model = 'iso' (bed::PointwiseIsostasy): the ice-equivalent load transmitted to the bed (compute_load: ice_load = H, ocean_load = (rho_sea_water/rho_ice)*max(sea_level-bed, 0), floating-ice load excluded), the instantaneous isostasy update topg_out = bed_in - f*(load - load_last) with f = rho_ice/rho_mantle and load_last <- load (PointwiseIsostasy has NO relaxation time: a load change is fully compensated in the single update that follows it), and the BedDef load-accumulator semantics: BedDef::update() accumulates load*dt on every call and only triggers update_impl() when t_final reaches the next update time (m_t_last + bed_deformation.update_interval), feeding it the time-averaged load m_load_accumulator/dt_beddef (the C++ scales by the reciprocal 1/dt_beddef) and then setting uplift = (topg - topg_last)/dt_beddef, topg_last = topg. The PointwiseIsostasyUpdate / ComputeLoad models are the pointwise laws (tested against stage1/dumps/bed/pointwise.csv at rel 1e-12); BedDefLoadAccumulator is the interval time average (the exact evaluation of the interval integral for the piecewise-constant driver history of stage1/dumps/bed/load_history.csv); PointwiseIsostasyTwoIntervals is the two-full-update-interval state trajectory (the columns.csv contract: bed_out_1 = -f*150 m, bed_out_2 = -f*300 m under the ice, no change where the load does not change). All shared math is imported by reference from ./bed_templates.esm. Deferred: bed_deformation.model = 'given' (Given), 'null' (Null), and 'lc' (LingleClark / LingleClarkSerial, the Fourier spectral-collocation viscous relaxation with mantle_viscosity and elastic lithosphere -- a future subassembly); the BedDef update_impl dispatch / accumulator state machine is represented here by the two-interval trace and the accumulator models because the inline-test runner integrates ODEs without event handling (esm-spec; the harness refuses models with discrete_events), and the PointwiseIsostasy update is instantaneous."
  },
  "models": {
    "ComputeLoad": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./bed_templates.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "bed": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "bedrock elevation (the C++ bed argument of compute_load; BedDef accumulates the load against m_topg_last, the bed at the start of the interval)"
        },
        "ice_thickness": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "ice thickness H (the load of grounded ice in ice-equivalent meters)"
        },
        "sea_level": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "sea level elevation (the C++ sea_level_elevation argument of compute_load)"
        },
        "rho_ice": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "default": 910.0,
          "description": "ice density (constants.ice.density)"
        },
        "rho_sea_water": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "default": 1028.0,
          "description": "sea water density (constants.sea_water.density)"
        },
        "ocean_depth": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "ocean depth max(sea_level - bed, 0)"
        },
        "ocean_load": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "seawater load expressed as ice-equivalent thickness (rho_sea_water/rho_ice)*ocean_depth"
        },
        "load": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "load on the bed expressed as ice-equivalent thickness (ice_load = H if H > ocean_load else 0; the load of floating ice is excluded)"
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "_comment": "compute_load: ocean_depth = max(sea_level - bed, 0).",
          "lhs": "ocean_depth",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "bed_ocean_depth",
            "args": [
              "sea_level",
              "bed"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "compute_load: ocean_load = (rho_sea_water/rho_ice)*ocean_depth.",
          "lhs": "ocean_load",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "bed_ocean_load",
            "args": [
              "rho_sea_water",
              "rho_ice",
              "ocean_depth"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "compute_load: return ice_load if ice_load > ocean_load else 0 (this excludes the load of ice shelves).",
          "lhs": "load",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "bed_load",
            "args": [
              "ice_thickness",
              "ocean_load"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "compute_load_tuple_1",
          "description": "compute_load(bed=-200 m, H=0 m, sea_level=0 m) with rho_ice=910, rho_sea_water=1028: ocean_depth = max(sea_level-bed, 0) = 200 m; load = H if H > (1028/910)*ocean_depth else 0 = 0 m (stage1/dumps/bed/pointwise.csv).",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 1.0
          },
          "parameter_overrides": {
            "bed": -200.0,
            "ice_thickness": 0.0,
            "sea_level": 0.0,
            "rho_ice": 910.0,
            "rho_sea_water": 1028.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "ocean_depth",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 200.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-12
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "load",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-12
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "compute_load_tuple_2",
